Ladybird refreshes the connected FontFace after descriptor removal.
Blink’s AbstractPropertySetCSSStyleDeclaration::removeProperty() calls
DidMutate(), and StyleRuleCSSStyleDeclaration::DidMutate() notifies the
stylesheet. WebKit’s PropertySetCSSDescriptors::removeProperty() also
calls didMutate(). Gecko’s CSSFontFaceRuleDecl::RemoveProperty() resets
the descriptor through Servo_FontFaceRule_ResetDescriptor(), without a
matching update notification there. Ladybird keeps the connected face
synchronized with the rule.

Ladybird refreshes a connected face after cssText replacement, keeping
its identity when src is unchanged. Blink notifies the stylesheet in
StyleRuleCSSStyleDeclaration::DidMutate(), and Chrome updates rendering
but replaces the connected object. WebKit calls didMutate() from
PropertySetCSSDescriptors::setCssText(). Gecko rejects cssText changes
in CSSFontFaceRuleDecl::SetCssText(). Ladybird preserves its connection
semantics: A changed src disconnects the old face and creates another.
